DEPENDENT SEQUENCES, i.e., several of phrases, or two or more which clauses or thaé clauses or -ly words, each of which is not parallel or opposed, but has a dependent relation, to the one before or after hie For the point of the distinction between dependent & parallel sequences, see -LY 3.
